    <!-- Help -->
    <!-- ============================== -->
    <string name="title_help">How to Use</string>
    <string name="help_getting_started_title">Getting Started</string>
    <string name="help_getting_started_body">1. Open any app with a text field (WhatsApp, Gmail, Chrome, etc.)\n2. Tap the field to bring up the keyboard.\n3. The floating mic button will appear over the keyboard.\n4. Tap it once to start recording.\n5. Tap again to stop — your speech gets typed into the field.</string>
    <string name="help_moving_title">Moving the Button</string>
    <string name="help_moving_body">• Long-press the button to unlock it.\n• Drag it anywhere on the screen.\n• Use the size slider to resize it.\n• Tap Done to lock it in place.\n\nOr open Settings → Reposition &amp; Resize Button.</string>
    <string name="help_tips_title">Tips</string>
    <string name="help_tips_body">• Speak clearly at a normal pace.\n• Short clips (under 30 seconds) work best.\n• If the text doesn\'t appear, it\'s been copied to your clipboard — just paste.\n• The button only shows when the keyboard is open.</string>
    <string name="help_trouble_title">Troubleshooting</string>
    <string name="help_trouble_body">• Button not appearing? Check that the Accessibility service is enabled.\n• Text not typing in? Some apps block auto-fill — the text is always copied to the clipboard as a backup.\n• Still stuck? Use Report an Issue from Settings so we can help.</string>

